From: phpv patch conversion <patches@phpv.invalid>
Subject: [0001-configure-curl-cflags] PHP 5.2-5.6: keep warning suppressions in the curl SSL conftest

PHP 5.x's generated configure clobbers CFLAGS during the
'checking for openssl support in libcurl' test with `curl-config --cflags`
output (just an -I path). The conftest uses strncasecmp() without
<strings.h>, a hard error on GCC 14+. Append warning suppressions to the
substitution so the test compiles clean.

The surrounding configure code differs across 5.2-5.6, so this patch uses
a single-line hunk that patch can locate by content in every version.
---
 a/configure | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -1 +1 @@
-    CFLAGS="`$CURL_CONFIG --cflags`"
+    CFLAGS="`$CURL_CONFIG --cflags` -Wno-implicit-function-declaration -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration"
-- 
2.47.1

